Asura @VERSION@ for Apple silicon, macOS 27 or later

Install with Homebrew (recommended):

    brew install --cask pidster/tap/asura

Homebrew puts Asura.app in /Applications and links the asura command.

Install by hand:

1. Drag Asura.app onto Applications.
2. Link the command into a folder on your PATH, for example:

     ln -s /Applications/Asura.app/Contents/MacOS/asura /opt/homebrew/bin/asura

3. In a new terminal, run: asura --version

Keep Asura.app whole in /Applications: do not copy the asura executable out
of the app. Asura keeps its state in ~/.asura. Removing Asura.app does not
remove ~/.asura.
